The first semantics draft is now in place: it parses the translator’s constructors, installs/calls functions, executes assignments/conditionals/string loops, and models the exact built-ins the submitted program uses. I also separated the reference encoder from the interpreter so the main proof compares execution against an independently defined character-by-character contract. I’m compiling now and will tighten the rules based on K’s parser/prover feedback.
Prompt and translator are understood; the Python implementation and generated AST are complete. Moving into compile/debug of the K definition.
