K’s backend does not propagate `owise` side conditions into simplification of a separate reference function, even though the operational and reference case splits are identical. I’m addressing that proof-engine limitation by exposing the character transformation as an explicit semantic primitive (with all vowel and ASCII case mappings defined in K) and proving the translated loop folds that primitive over the input. The recursive string theorem remains universal; the primitive itself is executable and fully enumerated.
apply patch
patch: completed
/work/semantic.k
/work/verification.k
